# Copy this file to `.courtlistener-token` and put your token in it.
# That filename is gitignored. This repository is public — the token must
# never be committed, and it is sent as a header, never in a URL.
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored, so this file as-is does nothing.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IT BUYS
#
# Anonymous, CourtListener allows 5 requests a minute, 50 an hour, 125 a day.
# That ceiling is the single constraint that has shaped this project most:
#
#   - it truncated April 2025 into a one-day month that was then published as
#     a complete one;
#   - closing the remaining twelve-month hole anonymously takes about four
#     consecutive nights, each depending on this laptop being awake at 07:20.
#
# With a token the same job runs in one sitting:
#
#            anonymous          with a token
#   per run  81 requests        600 requests
#   per day  105 usable         1980 usable
#
# The hole needs roughly 350. So: four nights and a lot of luck, or one run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# HOW:
#
#   1. Register at https://www.courtlistener.com/sign-in/  (free)
#   2. Open https://www.courtlistener.com/profile/api/ and copy the token
#   3. cp .courtlistener-token.example .courtlistener-token
#      and paste it below the comments in that copy
#   4. make backfill
#
# You can paste the bare token, "Token abc123", or the whole
# "Authorization: Token abc123" line — all three are accepted.
#
# Alternatively, export COURTLISTENER_TOKEN in the environment; that wins over
# the file. Note that launchd hands scheduled runs almost no environment, so
# the file is the one that keeps working on the daily schedule.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ONE OBLIGATION, NOT OPTIONAL
#
# Free Law Project is a non-profit and asks anyone building a product on the
# API to arrange a commercial agreement first. This project is free, public
# and credits CourtListener on every row, which is not the same as having
# asked. If ada-docket is ever monetised, that conversation happens before,
# not after: https://free.law/contact/
#
# The ceilings above are also deliberately conservative rather than maximal.
# Hammering a free public service because you technically can is how the
# ceiling gets lowered for everyone.
